# netsurf: a form's entries as HTML builds them -- line breaks, charsets,
# submitters, disabled fieldsets, dirname, _charset_ (patch 283)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 282)
#
# A <form> submitted without script goes through the engine's own form
# path (form_submit -> form_dom_to_data), which 257 left alone. Its body,
# compared with Chromium's for the same forms part by part (the gate
# server's /form-check, below), differed in what the entries were, for
# every enctype:
#
#  - line breaks: names and values are sent with CR LF (a textarea's
#    "line1\nline2" went as LF; a name's line break as %0A, Chromium's
#    %0D%0A). File names keep their bytes (the encoder escapes them).
#  - the charset: UTF-8 and the windows-1252 family (iso-8859-1, latin1,
#    us-ascii are its labels, per the Encoding Standard) are encoded here,
#    a character the encoding lacks as "&#N;" as HTML says; the Vita's
#    iconv-free converter treated windows-1252 as Latin-1 (the euro and
#    0x80-0x9F lost) and wrote "?" for the rest.
#  - a hidden input named _charset_ sends the encoding's name ("UTF-8",
#    "windows-1252"); it sent its own value.
#  - dirname: a text / search input or a textarea with a dirname attribute
#    adds "<dirname>=ltr|rtl" (its dir, an ancestor's, or "auto": the
#    value's first strong character).
#  - disabled: a control inside a disabled <fieldset> is disabled (not in
#    that fieldset's first legend); a disabled option, or one in a disabled
#    optgroup, is not sent. Only the element's own attribute counted.
#  - a control with an empty name is not sent.
#  - the submitter: only the button that submitted the form is sent. With
#    none -- form.submit(), requestSubmit() -- the first submit input or
#    button was taken as the submitter and sent. Implicit submission (Enter
#    in a field) now goes with the form's default button, and not at all
#    when that button is disabled (form_default_button, box_textarea.c).
#  - an image button activated without a pointer (requestSubmit, click(),
#    the keyboard) sends "name.x=0", "name.y=0" ("x", "y" when nameless);
#    with no click coordinates the whole submission was abandoned.
#  - an element type the code does not handle is skipped; it abandoned the
#    submission.
#
# Not changed: the multipart encoder itself (libcurl's mime API: a valid
# random boundary, names and filenames %-escaped for '"' CR LF, as
# Chromium), which already matched part for part once the entries did.
#
# Found on the way, not fixed: libhubbub turns "&#13;" into LF (the
# standard keeps CR), so a value written "a&#13;&#10;b" sends two line
# breaks; a script's textarea.value / input.value is the value attribute
# (the bridge's generic reflection), so a textarea's value set from script
# is not what is submitted; form.elements.namedItem is missing; a form's
# target naming an iframe navigates the whole window; a parsed iframe's
# contentWindow.document is undefined to its parent.
#
# Gate (with 284, 285): tools/run-vita-sim.sh "scriptless form
# submissions" -- nine submissions, each "FORMCHECK <case> ok <digest>"
# equal to Chromium's.
